ea6ed6f12fc04114bb705adb4a4ca145fcca8a024443d605ea23aa90a5ee09","event_uuid":"4a0df20e-d266-4779-b260-26c5541e40da","position":{"commit_sha":"d4e0c5f2c5145cd19e1ae2270185c7bb294c32fb","position":"1786051996662878001-4a0df20e-d266-4779-b260-26c5541e40da"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ddc4d7e715652a13fcef6a3b552f15ab64229058dd706b7ceb5f0b3f8077f2cb","event_uuid":"aa2d1f9a-e9e2-4768-bbbe-d0a4b889fc0b","position":{"commit_sha":"2ed8cb074ddceefab2f4b9ef49957ac1658e8b05","position":"1786052016443647001-aa2d1f9a-e9e2-4768-bbbe-d0a4b889fc0b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"969051adc43d53aae137d76ab46b8df5feb38fdf35f73504dbe57ce446695dd1","event_uuid":"7c7a3bf9-4940-4aec-811b-4fd5274a4125","position":{"commit_sha":"2ed8cb074ddceefab2f4b9ef49957ac1658e8b05","position":"1786052016944893001-7c7a3bf9-4940-4aec-811b-4fd5274a4125"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785991666034187001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f9984863-0ac5-4b02-bf62-1121cc40df77","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97"},{"link_uuid":"4a0df20e-d266-4779-b260-26c5541e40da","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e0f0-a1ae-59fb-4730"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe completion-verification close gate chronically fails in ways that leave no verdict: runaway duplicate tool-call loops (one live run repeated an identical search_files call 144x), request-budget exhaustion that dies verdict-less (the --force-close trap: a resource exhaustion is not a verdict, and the gate's only documented exit is --force-close), a recovery path that fans out one isolated evidence run per criterion (operator-ruled unapproved: c9f7's shape is 22 criteria x 20-request budget = 440 requests worst case with ~2.67M context chars re-sent), and a flat 100,000-char recovery context bound (completion_recovery.py:68) that refuses the live 121,147-char ticket c9f7 forever because ticket context is append-only and can only grow. Each failure was patched separately across four exhausted close attempts on epic e369; this epic reworks the verifier's context management as one design so exhaustion is bounded, verified progress survives failures, and every run with progress ends in a scored, signed verdict.\n\n## Approach\n\nRework along seams that already exist, generalizing only where multiple LLM workflows already share code (the agent_call.py tool-wrapping seam armed for every tool-bearing run, and model_classes.py model knowledge); everything specific to completion semantics — the verdict bank, criterion identity, context assembly, verdict coverage — stays completion-local in the workflow modules. Child responsibilities, each delivered by one child:\n\n- **Context ceilings** — replace the flat recovery char bound with a physical ceiling derived from the resolved verifier model's own context window plus an economic ceiling bounding total re-send spend, preserving the d59e invariants (no elision, zero billable calls on refusal).\n- **Duplicate-call damping** — memoize duplicate read-only tool calls at the shared agent-call seam and steer the model off repeats with static nudges; the shipped distinct-ratio runaway actuator stays as the abort backstop.\n- **Banked, batched verification** — record per-criterion verdicts incrementally to a run-scoped bank; replace the per-criterion recovery fan-out with batched successor runs over the unverified remainder under a request-denominated budget pool; finalize to a full-coverage verdict whenever any progress is banked, with a deterministic no-LLM fallback so a run with banked progress can never die verdict-less.\n- **Context pre-loading** — pre-fetch ranked file_impact contents into the fenced verifier context under a budget clamp with a per-file full/skeleton manifest, cutting agentic read round-trips (live traces show 67-82% of distinct file reads are covered by subtree file_impact).\n- **Interim evidence-run insurance** — single-criterion evidence-run survival hardening that ships only while the fan-out it patches still exists.\n\nSequencing is encoded as dependency edges: ceilings first (smallest change; unblocks re-certifications refused at preflight today), then duplicate-call damping (immediate waste cut for every agentic workflow), then the banked/batched core rework, then pre-loading (its improvement is only measurable against the post-rework baseline).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A completion verification whose primary run dies in a typed failure (budget exhaustion, runaway loop, or token exhaustion) with at least one criterion verdict banked ends in a full-coverage verdict instead of a verdict-less error — delivered by the banked-verification child; checked by its unit suite and a live Bedrock run recorded on that child.\n- [ ] No completion code path launches one isolated LLM run per criterion — delivered by the banked-verification child; checked by grep over src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py showing the fan-out removed, plus its unit suite.\n- [ ] The recovery preflight accepts the live c9f7 shape (121,147 chars x 22 criteria) under the two-ceiling bound with the d59e invariants intact — delivered by the context-ceilings child; checked by its held-out unit oracle and a live run recorded on that child.\n- [ ] Duplicate read-only tool calls inside one agentic run are served from a memo with a static nudge instead of re-executing, with the runaway actuator's window math unchanged — delivered by the duplicate-call damping child; checked by its unit tests and a live Bedrock capture recorded on that child.\n- [ ] The completion verifier's context pre-loads ranked file_impact contents with a full/skeleton manifest and reduces live request counts by at least 20% with verdict class unchanged versus the post-rework baseline — delivered by the pre-loading child; checked per that child's live A/B acceptance criteria.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e0f0-a1ae-59fb-4730"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"aa2d1f9a-e9e2-4768-bbbe-d0a4b889fc0b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Rework completion-verifier context management: batched AC verification, context ceilings, pre-loading","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4e28c48a-3c9e-4819-8c2f-ee5a3a9590f3","f9984863-0ac5-4b02-bf62-1121cc40df77","ea806697-6429-4865-ba16-9a6b1f27288d","d8d3c161-7bb2-444b-961c-d7bc9df055fe","4a0df20e-d266-4779-b260-26c5541e40da","aa2d1f9a-e9e2-4768-bbbe-d0a4b889fc0b","7c7a3bf9-4940-4aec-811b-4fd5274a4125"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786052016944893002,"uuid":"df1c4208-0fd5-4d09-a2b0-f6f0a00063dc"}